<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The DEV depth archive (ES Level Absorption Requirements section 9, items 1 and 6; ES Book Liquidity Walls
  Requirements rev 11 section 8): oe-archive-depth.sh runs oe-archive-kafka.sh with ENV=dev and
  TOPICS="$OE_DEPTH_TOPICS_dev" (oe-topics.env: es.rithmic.depth, underlying.es.trades.linearized,
  futures.liquidity-wall.closures, es.rithmic.mbo) against the dev broker and the dev schema registry, four times a day.

  WHY FOUR TIMES, AND WHY HERE. es.rithmic.depth carries a 12-hour retention on dev, so a once-a-day pass
  loses half of every session; every six hours, one missed run costs nothing. It is a dedicated job on the
  dev Mac, separate from the nightly 17:10 ET run on .252 (document A section 9 item 6), and it is registered
  for DEV ONLY — nothing here reads prod or es4.

  THE SCHEDULE IS IN THE HOST'S LOCAL TIME. launchd has no CRON_TZ; StartCalendarInterval fires at the wall
  clock of the Mac it runs on. The dev Mac runs on America/New_York, which is the same assumption the
  watchdog beside this file makes for its 07:00 ET, so the four entries below are 02:00, 08:00, 14:00 and
  20:00 ET. If the host's zone ever changes, these drift with it — convert them, or pin the host to New York.
  Ordinary daylight-saving switches are harmless: launchd follows the local clock, so 02:00 stays 02:00 ET.

  Install: run scripts/ops/archive/install-dev-mac-depth-archive.sh. Do NOT copy files by hand — the installer
  owns the list of files the wrapper and the archiver read from beside themselves, refuses to install while the
  canonical archive helper jar and the contracts jar are not beside them (the Avro depth and closure topics cannot
  be captured without them), verifies the staged copy under launchd's own environment, and fails unless exactly
  one agent registers. The dry-run flag is spelled out in the installer's header.

  scripts/ci/validate-dev-mac-depth-archive.sh checks that this file, the installer and the wrapper still agree.

  ARCHIVE_DIR is deliberately NOT set here (BZ 360, as for the watchdog): the wrapper resolves the root from
  ARCHIVE_ROOT_CANDIDATES and requires the NAS sentinel in it. Set it here only to override that on a host
  where the candidates are wrong.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.optionsedge.oe-archive-depth</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/abhinav/oe-ops/oe-archive-depth.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>2</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>8</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>14</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>20</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
  </array>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/abhinav/oe-ops/archive-depth.launchd.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/abhinav/oe-ops/archive-depth.launchd.err.log</string>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
</dict>
</plist>
